      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This was mentioned in a Dev Update. They were going to move the blocks and mutes from the servers to your local drive. If I remember correctly there was a week window when if you logged in then they would move the data from the servers to the local drive. Once that window ended they deleted the data from the servers.\n\nIt seems you didn't log in during that week.\n\nAlso if you reinstall windows, or switch PCs, or just wipe the VRC data then you'll lose the blocks and mutes too. Which is not a pleasant surprise.\n\nPersonally I think that a week window was way way too short. The transition window should have been a lot longer. Maybe they could have just kept it but use is exclusively for offloading the data to the user's drive whenever they would log in for the first time",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
